{"id": "EUVD-2026-86858", "enisaUuid": "571701b4-9feb-3e7b-bd73-41670dcf2f26", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: fix unit conversions in per_binval computation\n\nLOLLM noticed that we're doing the unit conversion in the per_binval\ncomputation backwards -- xfs_buf_inval_log_space's second parameter is\nsupposed to be in bytes, but max_binval is in units of fsblocks.  Hence\nthe conversion should be FSB -> B, not the other way around.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:13", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5089a328acc83fe2f23127a79397a0bfd9ebc33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cfeba3bdf4dfa405e29f4ee13a20e9063fd0b7ef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/05cff7c2b79f76c7cfe90613a60e16aaaa051ef7"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97550", "GHSA-j93m-m3f2-m54f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c61b11e-b0ce-36b3-9544-0f36f251a16c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "28e1f673-59f5-3458-862d-11fdafb8eac1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "3b9336bc-76e8-3048-84d8-4d2ad34f795f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2311ec6778fcde9d40cd9e22899f8bd594d8465 <b5089a328acc83fe2f23127a79397a0bfd9ebc33"}, {"id": "51345373-25f3-356a-bd94-958f658430a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "62f40234-f1c3-32d2-97fb-edc45b866937", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2311ec6778fcde9d40cd9e22899f8bd594d8465 <05cff7c2b79f76c7cfe90613a60e16aaaa051ef7"}, {"id": "a2da58f4-8e45-33df-9a66-81c8c94be48d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b2311ec6778fcde9d40cd9e22899f8bd594d8465 <cfeba3bdf4dfa405e29f4ee13a20e9063fd0b7ef"}, {"